re 75 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.690 euros, se adjudicó en noviembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que muchos contratos estén cerca del límite no indica que haya sido un error. Puede deberse a razones legítimas, como necesidades específicas o precios del mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se ajustan a presupuestos cerrados o a nuevas necesidades.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 137 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 23.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.5 to 7.4. December accounts for 9% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 10. Contract [1], for 14,690 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market conditions or budget constraints. Statistical trends alone do not indicate wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the distribution of contracts across different sectors to see if any area is overrepresented. Review the terms of contract [1] to ensure compliance with legal thresholds. Verify if multiple contracts served the same purpose to avoid overprocurement.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["VGfOViQjKE4%2Bk2oCbDosIw%3D%3D","lXJHUhqb0ly5HQrHoP3G5A%3D%3D","DQTaaNh6S1yS81gZFETWmA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}